window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-c302b8efa03eab38"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"appshots\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"appshot\">Appshot 截图</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code> 可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>Appshot 可以将当前位于最前面的应用窗口发送到 ChatGPT 聊天中。当你正在电脑上的其他应用里工作，并希望把当前上下文提供给 ChatGPT 以便它协助处理任务时，可以使用 Appshot。</p> <p>macOS 和 Windows 上的 ChatGPT 桌面应用均支持 Appshot。在 macOS 上同时按下两个 Command 键，在 Windows 上同时按下两个 Alt 键即可截取一次。你也可以为 Appshot 设置自定义快捷键。</p> <p><a id=\"what-appshots-capture\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"appshot_1\">Appshot 会捕获什么</h2> <p>Appshot 只捕获最前面的窗口。捕获内容可以包括：</p> <ul> <li>当前窗口的可见图像。</li> <li>该窗口可提供的文本，包括当前可见文本，以及应用在可见滚动区域之外提供的文本。</li> </ul> <p>将 Appshot 添加到聊天后，它的行为与附件相同。与手动附加的文件或图像一样，ChatGPT 会将 Appshot 保存在本地会话文件中。</p> <p><a id=\"when-to-use-appshots\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"appshot_2\">何时使用 Appshot</h2> <p>当 ChatGPT 需要先了解另一个应用中的上下文才能采取行动时，可以使用 Appshot。</p> <p>例如：</p> <ul> <li>分享 API 参考页面，并请 ChatGPT 编写使用该 API 的脚本。</li> <li>分享邮件或日历视图，并请 ChatGPT 草拟下一步内容。</li> <li>分享图像编辑器、设计稿或预览窗口，并请 ChatGPT 修改相关资源或代码。</li> <li>分享错误信息、设置面板或应用状态；这些内容用截图展示会比文字描述更方便。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"take-an-appshot\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"appshot_3\">截取 Appshot</h2> <ol> <li>将你想分享的应用窗口置于最前面。</li> <li>在 macOS 上同时按下两个 Command 键，在 Windows 上同时按下两个 Alt 键；也可以使用你在 ChatGPT 设置中配置的自定义快捷键。</li> <li>如果 ChatGPT 要求设置权限，请完成设置。</li> <li>告诉 ChatGPT 如何处理这张 Appshot。</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT 聊天输入框中附有 Appshot 截图和后续提示</p> </blockquote> <p>默认情况下，ChatGPT 会为 Appshot 开始一个新聊天。如果你在最近 60 秒内与某个聊天进行过交互，ChatGPT 会将 Appshot 添加到该最近聊天中。连续截取 Appshot 时，后续截图会添加到同一个聊天中。</p> <p>你可以在应用设置中更改快捷键和<strong>Appshot 目标位置</strong>。选择<strong>当前聊天</strong>或<strong>新聊天</strong>来指定目标，也可以保留<strong>自动</strong>，采用上述行为。</p> <p><a id=\"use-appshots-with-mini\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"use-appshots-from-the-floating-controls\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"appshot_4\">从浮动控件使用 Appshot</h3> <p>在 macOS 上，如果<a href=\"#/article/a-74fe1167725e9c4d?sectionMissing=app-send-appshots-to-your-pet\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">浮动宠物控件（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-74fe1167725e9c4d\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>已打开，而 ChatGPT 主窗口处于后台，选择<strong>自动</strong>后，这些控件会通过 Appshot 开始一个新聊天。选择<strong>迷你</strong>作为宠物时也适用。请先在主应用中完成 Appshot 权限设置。在 Windows 上，Appshot 会在主应用中打开。</p> <p><a id=\"permissions-and-safety\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">权限与安全</h2> <p>在 macOS 上，ChatGPT 可能会在截取 Appshot 之前要求以下权限：</p> <ul> <li><strong>屏幕与系统音频录制</strong>：允许 ChatGPT 捕获最前面窗口的图像。</li> <li><strong>辅助功能</strong>：允许 ChatGPT 读取最前面窗口可提供的文本。</li> </ul> <p>截取 Appshot 会将捕获的图像和可用文本分享给 ChatGPT。除非任务确实需要，否则请避免截取包含敏感内容的窗口。</p> <p>请像检查要分享给 ChatGPT 的屏幕截图和文档那样，检查 Appshot 的内容。</p> <p><a id=\"limits-and-troubleshooting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">限制与故障排除</h2> <p>Appshot 需要在 macOS 或 Windows 上使用 ChatGPT 桌面应用。如果你在 CLI 中恢复一个已包含 Appshot 的聊天，该附件会保留在聊天历史中，但 CLI 无法创建新的 Appshot。</p> <p>对于某些应用和网站，包括 Google Docs、Gmail、Google Sheets 和 Google Slides，ChatGPT 可能只能收到可见的屏幕截图，而无法收到完整文档或屏幕之外的文本。在 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex 中，ChatGPT 可以使用已安装且匹配的插件来访问相关应用内容，并协助处理你的请求。</p> <p>如果 Appshot 无法正常工作，请更新桌面应用、检查所配置的快捷键，并确认你的组织允许使用 Appshot。在 macOS 上还要检查权限：</p> <ol> <li>打开<strong>系统设置 &gt; 隐私与安全性</strong>。</li> <li>在“屏幕与系统音频录制”和“辅助功能”中检查 Codex Computer Use 是否已获授权。</li> <li>重新启动应用，然后重试。</li> </ol>","en":"<h1 id=\"appshots\">Appshots</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Appshots let you send the frontmost app window to a chat in ChatGPT. Use them when you're actively working in another app on your computer and want to provide ChatGPT with your current context so it can help you with the task.</p> <p>Appshots are available in the ChatGPT desktop app on macOS and Windows. Press both Command keys on macOS or both Alt keys on Windows to take one. You can also configure a custom Appshots hotkey.</p> <h2 id=\"what-appshots-capture\">What appshots capture</h2> <p>An appshot captures the frontmost window only. It can include:</p> <ul> <li>An image of the visible window.</li> <li>Available text from that window, including visible text and text the app makes available outside the visible scroll area.</li> </ul> <p>After you add an appshot to a chat, it behaves like an attachment. ChatGPT stores appshots locally in the session file, like files or images you attach manually.</p> <h2 id=\"when-to-use-appshots\">When to use appshots</h2> <p>Use appshots when ChatGPT needs context from another app before it can act.</p> <p>Examples:</p> <ul> <li>Share an API reference page and ask ChatGPT to write a script that uses it.</li> <li>Share an email or calendar view and ask ChatGPT to draft the next step.</li> <li>Share an image editor, design, or preview window and ask ChatGPT to revise the related assets or code.</li> <li>Share an error, settings panel, or app state that's easier to show than describe.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"take-an-appshot\">Take an appshot</h2> <ol> <li>Bring the app window you want to share to the front.</li> <li>Press both Command keys on macOS or both Alt keys on Windows, or use the custom hotkey you configured in ChatGPT settings.</li> <li>Complete the permission setup if ChatGPT asks.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to perform a task with the appshot.</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT chat composer with an Appshot attachment and follow-up prompt</p> </blockquote> <p>By default, ChatGPT starts a new chat for the appshot. If you interacted with a chat in the last 60 seconds, ChatGPT adds the appshot to that recent chat instead. Taking consecutive appshots adds them to the same chat.</p> <p>You can change the hotkey and <strong>Appshot destination</strong> in the app settings. Choose <strong>Current chat</strong> or <strong>New chat</strong> to set a destination, or keep <strong>Automatic</strong> for the behavior described here.</p> <p><a id=\"use-appshots-with-mini\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"use-appshots-from-the-floating-controls\">Use appshots from the floating controls</h3> <p>On macOS, when the <a href=\"#/article/a-74fe1167725e9c4d?sectionMissing=app-send-appshots-to-your-pet\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">floating pet controls (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-74fe1167725e9c4d\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> are open and the main ChatGPT window is in the background, <strong>Automatic</strong> starts a new chat from those controls with the appshot. This also works when you select <strong>Mini</strong> as your pet. Complete Appshots permission setup in the main app first. On Windows, Appshots open in the main app.</p> <h2 id=\"permissions-and-safety\">Permissions and safety</h2> <p>On macOS, ChatGPT may ask for these permissions before it can take appshots:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Screen &amp; System Audio Recording</strong> lets ChatGPT capture an image of the frontmost window.</li> <li><strong>Accessibility</strong> lets ChatGPT read available text from the frontmost window.</li> </ul> <p>Taking an appshot shares the captured image and available text with ChatGPT. Avoid taking appshots of sensitive content unless the task requires that content.</p> <p>Review appshots the same way you would review sharing screenshots and documents with ChatGPT.</p> <h2 id=\"limits-and-troubleshooting\">Limits and troubleshooting</h2> <p>Appshots require the ChatGPT desktop app on macOS or Windows. If you resume a chat in the CLI that already contains an appshot, the attachment is part of the chat history, but the CLI can't create a new appshot.</p> <p>For some apps and websites, including Google Docs, Gmail, Google Sheets, and Google Slides, ChatGPT may receive only the visible screenshot and may not receive the full document or off-screen text. In ChatGPT Work or Codex, ChatGPT can use a matching installed plugin to access the relevant app content and help with your request.</p> <p>If appshots don't work, update the desktop app, check the configured hotkey, and confirm that your organization allows Appshots. On macOS, also check permissions:</p> <ol> <li>Open <strong>System Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security</strong>.</li> <li>Check <strong>Screen &amp; System Audio Recording</strong> and <strong>Accessibility</strong> for Codex Computer Use.</li> <li>Restart the app and try again.</li> </ol>"};
